msgid "A changed address reaches the account only through the `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync` timer or a deploy: `files/python/apply/rbac_roles.py` renames the account, while `files/python/infinito_rbac/infinito_rbac/login.py` refuses the sign-in until then, up to 15 minutes. Cause: `frappe.rename_doc` takes no `ignore_permissions`, and `User.after_rename` renames the user's `Notification Settings` with a permission check the Guest session of the callback fails (read in frappe v16.51.0 `frappe/__init__.py`, `frappe/core/doctype/user/user.py`, not measured). Options: rename in `login.py` under `frappe.set_user(\"Administrator\")`, which also clears `frappe.local.form_dict` of the request. A member bound to two accounts, or whose former account another member now holds by address, gets neither renamed."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "A changed module reaches whoever imports it, transitively, and whoever names it as a string (``python -m utils.x`` in a task); a package's ``__main__`` answers to the package name. Any other file reaches whoever names its path, by the repository path or a shorter tail of it, and its siblings that name it by file name, and whoever builds a path into its directory from a variable (``<dir>/${lint_type}.sh``); such a dispatcher passes the walk on only to the lines that hand it the value naming the file. A plugin reaches whoever calls one of its names; a group_vars key reaches whoever reads it, a key of another group_vars file included. The walk ends at a role (a seed), a test (T0), a Makefile target of :data:`TOOLING_TARGETS` (T0), deploy machinery, a global deploy file, a workflow, any other Makefile target or a file of unknown kind (the full set), and at tooling nobody names. Deploy machinery is what the deploy targets run: :data:`surface.DEPLOY_MACHINERY` by its path and every module or script a Makefile target outside :data:`TOOLING_TARGETS` names, such as ``cli.meta.cache`` of ``make dotenv`` or ``cli.meta.ci.swarm_preflight`` of ``make swarm-zombie``."
msgstr ""

