msgid "A member of ``site-owner`` administers the site ``<username>.<parent>``, where ``domains.served`` in the Multisite variant sets the parent to ``user.blog.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>``. Only a Keycloak username (``[a-z1-9]``, or the agent form ``<4 chars>0<suffix>``) of at most 63 characters that is no WordPress ``illegal_names`` entry names a site. The mapper creates the site on the member’s first SSO login, records the member’s OIDC subject on it and only ever takes over or archives a site that carries that subject or that the deploy reserved for the login. An SSO login outside the group archives the site and keeps its content, a login back in the group restores it. A deploy applies a membership change as well: `tasks/05_site_owners.yml <tasks/05_site_owners.yml>`__ archives every own site whose login is no longer an inventory member and ends that member’s sessions."
