# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A practical long-term target is:"
msgstr "Sebuah target jangka panjang praktis adalah:"

msgid "A pre-flight check probes a host before a deploy changes it and stops the deploy when the host is in a state the deploy cannot recover from on its own: a kernel without its modules, a full disk, a docker object that belongs to another project, a port a host service already holds, or a domain that does not resolve."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix cannot judge the container, so the probe keeps the verdict and the prefix only ever RAISES a timing -- the composed start period is the longest of the two, never the prefix's alone. Lowering it once would have cut a fifteen minute start window down to two."
msgstr "Sebuah awalan tidak dapat menilai wadah, sehingga probe menyimpan putusan dan awalan hanya pernah RAISES waktu - periode awal yang terdiri adalah terpanjang dari keduanya, tidak pernah prefix sendirian. Menurunkan sekali akan memotong lima belas menit mulai jendela ke dua."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix does something on the way past -- sending a smoke mail is the only one so far -- and deliberately cannot decide liveness. That separation is what lets a probe stay the single verdict."
msgstr "Sebuah awalan melakukan sesuatu dalam perjalanan ke masa lalu -- mengirim sebuah surat asap adalah satu-satunya yang sejauh ini -- dan dengan sengaja tidak dapat memutuskan keleluasaan. Pemisahan itulah yang membuat probe tetap dalam putusan tunggal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix mask leaves a contiguous run of low bits free, so per octet the addresses span exactly ``network_address`` to ``broadcast_address``. The cross product of those four ranges is the network, which makes the octet decomposition exact for any prefix length, aligned or not."
msgstr "Sebuah topeng awalan meninggalkan run kontiguous bit rendah bebas, sehingga per oktet rentang alamat persis ``network_address`` ke ``broadcast_address``. Produk silang dari empat range adalah jaringan, yang membuat octet dekomposisi tepat untuk panjang prefix, selaras atau tidak."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A priority entry may pin axes (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), and the pin rides along into the retrigger: the entry never ran, so the run holds no evidence that the axes it named were the wrong ones. Only the name in front of the axis suffix is resolved against the statuses."
msgstr "Sebuah entri prioritas dapat pin sumbu (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), dan pin naik sepanjang ke pemicu: entri tidak pernah berlari, sehingga menjalankan memegang tidak ada bukti bahwa kapak itu bernama adalah yang salah. Hanya nama di depan akhiran sumbu diselesaikan terhadap status."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A priority role can fall behind the discovery budget cut in every mode, so the run holds no job for it and :func:`failed_roles` cannot see it — it is neither green nor red, it simply never ran. Carrying it into the retrigger is the only way it ever gets deployed."
msgstr "Peran prioritas bisa jatuh di belakang anggaran penemuan dipotong dalam setiap mode, sehingga menjalankan memegang ada pekerjaan untuk itu dan :func:`failed_roles` tidak bisa melihatnya - itu tidak hijau atau merah, hanya tidak pernah berlari. Membawa ke dalam retrigger adalah satu-satunya cara itu pernah akan dikerahkan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A privacy-first foundation for enterprises running AI locally and keeping sensitive data on-prem."
msgstr "Sebuah yayasan utama untuk perusahaan yang menjalankan AI lokal dan menjaga data sensitif pada Prem."

msgid "A process stuck in `D` cannot be killed and is the host-visible trace of a wedged mount. Only the state field is evaluated; the command name is never retained, so the count can be logged without leaking process command lines. The comm field may itself contain spaces and `)`, so the state is read after the last closing parenthesis rather than by index."
msgstr ""

msgid "A process that renders network-bound URLs once (one callback, one config) serves a single network, so an application served on several networks runs one such process per network."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A professional collaboration and identity management stack for modern organizations."
msgstr "Kolaborasi profesional dan manajemen identitas untuk organisasi modern."

msgid "A profile change made in Keycloak reaches Nextcloud on the next run of `files/python/ldap_refresh.py` (deploy or RBAC timer), a native LDAP login or the `user_ldap` background sync, not at the OIDC login itself: `oidc_login` in LDAP proxy mode fetches the DN without attributes (read from `LoginService::getLDAPUserUid` and `Access::fetchListOfUsers`), and no Playwright scenario can wait for a timer run. Options: an upstream `oidc_login` change that refreshes the LDAP record at login."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prompt above the server's state limit is truncated rather than rejected as a routing failure"
msgstr "Sebuah prompt di atas batas negara server dipotong daripada ditolak sebagai routing gagal"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prose deprecation value is not read as a date"
msgstr "Nilai deprekasi prosa tidak dibaca sebagai tanggal"

msgid "A provider declares ``overlay.stream_relay`` with a ``switch`` and the ``ports`` it opens. While the switch is true and the reverse proxy's own overlay applies in the mode, the provider and the reverse proxy share ``<entity>-relay`` and nothing else does, so the relay never puts the proxy on the provider's overlay with its consumers."
msgstr ""

msgid "A provider declares `overlay.stream_relay` in its `meta/networks.yml` with a `switch` (a config path on the provider), the `ports` it relays and the `subnet` of the relay network. While the switch is true, and only in the modes where the reverse proxy (`svc-prx-openresty`) itself runs on overlays (its own `networks.overlay.modes`, today `[swarm]`), the provider and the reverse proxy join a dedicated network `<entity>-relay` (`openldap-relay`), and no other role joins it. The provider carries its entity name as alias there. The reverse proxy never joins the provider's overlay. In compose openresty keeps the host network and reaches the published loopback port as before."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A provider writes its credential to the token store during its own role run, and each client resolves the providers it may reach from that store. This role runs at the end of the server stage, after every provider has written and before the end-to-end tests read the converged state."
msgstr "Seorang penyedia menulis kredensial ke toko token selama menjalankan perannya sendiri, dan setiap klien menyelesaikan penyedia yang mungkin didapat dari toko itu. Peran ini berjalan di akhir tahap server, setelah setiap penyedia telah ditulis dan sebelum akhir-ke-akhir tes membaca keadaan berkumpul."

msgid "A proving line carries the marker and a run token (``✓``/passed) and is not a skip line; a line that only skips the marker (a leading ``-`` or the word ``skipped``) does not count, so a guarded spec reported as skipped is not mistaken for executed."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A proxy repo that holds a cached copy serves it when its remote is unreachable, regardless of `metadataMaxAge` (measured). `autoBlock` is therefore off: while a remote is auto-blocked Nexus answers `404 Remote Auto Blocked` instead of falling back to that cached copy. The mirror repos below only come into play when nothing is cached either."
msgstr "Repo proksi yang memuat salinan cache melayani ketika remote tidak dapat dicapai, terlepas dari `metadataMaxAge` (diukur). `autoBlock` besocause is off: while a remote is auto-blocked Nexus answers `404 Remote Auto Blocked` Alih-alih jatuh kembali ke salinan cache. Repos cermin di bawah ini hanya datang ke dalam bermain ketika tidak ada cache baik."

msgid "A pull request labelled as touching protected paths is never recommended for merge; the review names the touched paths and leaves the decision to a human."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pull stages every declared role in a work directory outside ``roles/`` and checks it before the first entry of ``roles/`` changes, so a refused pull leaves ``roles/`` as it was. A pull or clean only ever replaces or removes the directories the pull placed itself, whose marker names them."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pull stages every role outside `roles/` and changes `roles/` only when all of them passed, so a refused pull leaves it as it was. It replaces or removes only the directories it placed itself, whose marker names them, and refuses a declared name that meets a symbolic link, a hand-placed directory or a copy of a placed role. `make roles-clean` removes every `roles/web-app-cst-*` directory the pull placed and reports every other one it leaves in place. Git ignores `roles/web-app-cst-*`, so a pulled role never enters a core commit."
msgstr ""

msgid "A pull stops while any of these files cannot be read: a declaration it cannot see would make it remove the role as no longer declared."
msgstr ""

msgid "A quality gate outranks both crons: while the machine's gate lock is held, the translator stays paused, at night as well, and resumes when the lock is released."
msgstr ""

msgid "A quality gate outranks every long-running job on the same machine (translation, deploys, builds, other gates): before the gate starts, the gate routine takes the machine's gate lock and pauses every running long job (the translation lane through `make i18n-pause`); after the gate ends, it releases the lock and resumes them. No agent writes to the tree under test while the gate runs. A gate that ran with a long job beside it is discarded, not judged."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A question MUST NOT modify files, code, or state. Only explicit commands MAY."
msgstr "Sebuah pertanyaan HARUS TIDAK mengubah berkas, kode, atau keadaan. Hanya perintah MAY eksplisit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A random bearer key per agent, known only to the broker, used in both directions."
msgstr "Sebuah kunci acak per agen, hanya diketahui broker, yang digunakan di kedua arah."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A rapid deployment stack for startups building software products and services."
msgstr "Tumpukan penyebaran cepat untuk startup membangun produk perangkat lunak dan jasa."

msgid "A re-entrant call returns before ``_MERGED_APPLICATIONS_CACHE`` is written, because its payload carries no users and keeps its volumes. It is therefore memoised on the render guard instead, which drops it when the guard releases. Without that, one template render recomputed the payload for every ``lookup('applications')`` it made."
msgstr ""

msgid "A read without a templar (the raw users inside an applications render) never takes the carrier."
msgstr ""

msgid "A readable injected sheet lets LibreTranslate rewrite the shared sheet's `prefers-color-scheme` at load; keep the injected links without `crossorigin` and shield such apps in the role `design.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid "A real upstream or licence limit keeps the item open with its reason; no workaround."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST NOT be written for a choice that a reader can recover from the code alone, such as a helper's signature or a local refactoring."
msgstr "Sebuah rekaman HARUS TIDAK ditulis untuk pilihan bahwa pembaca dapat pulih dari kode saja, seperti tanda tangan pembantu atau refaktoring lokal."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST be numbered in the order it was accepted, and its number MUST NOT be reused."
msgstr "Sebuah rekaman HARUS dinomori dalam urutan yang diterima, dan nomor HARUS TIDAK digunakan kembali."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST cover a decision whose reversal would be expensive: a contract between components, a data or naming shape other code depends on, or a rule that governs a whole subsystem."
msgstr "Sebuah rekaman HARUS menutupi keputusan yang pembalikan akan mahal: kontrak antara komponen, data atau bentuk penamaan lain tergantung pada, atau aturan yang mengatur seluruh subsistem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST describe the decision as it stands today, including the alternatives that were weighed and why they lost, so a later reader can tell a deliberate constraint from an accident."
msgstr "Sebuah rekaman HARUS menggambarkan keputusan karena berdiri hari ini, termasuk alternatif-alternatif yang ditimbang dan mengapa mereka kehilangan, sehingga pembaca kemudian dapat memberitahu hambatan disengaja dari kecelakaan."

msgid "A record newer than the image stops the deploy and leaves the volume untouched."
msgstr ""

msgid "A recover mirrors a snapshot into a live target directory (``rsync -aHAX --delete``), so the target's current state would be lost without a net. The flow therefore first runs the role's deployed backup service (``systemctl start`` on the role's unit), which applies the usual differential backup logic to the live data before anything is overwritten. Roles subclass :class:`DirectoryRecovery`, set ``unit_pattern`` and ship a thin ``files/python/recover.py`` CLI around it (enforced by ``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_bkp_roles_have_recover.py``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "A recurring property of these extensions is that many of them exist **only to bridge into another role**: `ldapauth` and `user_ldap` bridge to `svc-db-openldap`; `sociallogin`, `oidc-authenticator`, `OpenIDConnect`, `plg_system_keycloak`, and the WordPress OIDC plugin bridge to the SSO provider (`web-app-keycloak`); `wp-discourse` bridges to `web-app-discourse`; XWiki's `ai-llm` extension bridges to `web-app-litellm`. Today that bridge is implicit. This requirement makes it explicit: **an addon that bridges to another role MUST declare the bridged service, and that service MUST be present in the role's `meta/services.yml`.**"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A red job could not be reproduced by re-running its sweep, which is the property the whole rotation exists to provide."
msgstr "Pekerjaan merah tidak dapat direproduksi dengan menjalankan ulang sapuan, yang merupakan properti seluruh rotasi ada untuk menyediakan."

msgid "A redeploy of an unchanged version includes [`03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml`](./tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml) instead, which updates apps without querying the appstore:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A redeploy of an unchanged version includes ```03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml`` <./tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade/02_cached_updates.yml>`__ instead, which updates apps without querying the appstore:"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A refusal names the token and why. Fix the token, never the check: a variant that no longer exists means the list was carried over from an older run, and dropping the pin only moves the wrong row into the queue."
msgstr "Penolakan nama token dan mengapa. Perbaiki token, jangan pernah cek: varian yang tidak ada lagi berarti daftar tersebut dibawa dari run yang lebih tua, dan menjatuhkan pin hanya memindahkan baris yang salah ke dalam antrian."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A refusal records what the server answered under the masking of the day. A source change clears it by itself, because the entry is then new; a change to the masking or to the damage predicate does not, and those entries would stay skipped forever."
msgstr "Penolakan mencatat apa jawaban server di bawah masking hari. Sebuah perubahan sumber membersihkannya dengan sendirinya, karena entri kemudian baru; perubahan ke masking atau untuk prediksi kerusakan tidak, dan mereka entri akan tetap melewatkan selamanya."

msgid "A refused answer reaches the next engine"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A regex over dotted octets, e.g. ``192\\.168\\.24\\.\\d+`` for a /24 or ``192\\.168\\.(24|25)\\.\\d+`` for a /23."
msgstr "A regex over dotted octets, mis. ``192\\.168\\.24\\.\\d+`` untuk /24 atau ``192\\.168\\.(24|25)\\.\\d+`` untuk /23."

msgid "A release tag (``vX.Y.Z``) is built the first time someone opens it. The browser shows a progress bar and reloads once the build is done. Tags never change, so a tag is built again only after the cap in point 6 dropped it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A release tag (`vX.Y.Z`) is built the first time someone opens it. The browser shows a progress bar and reloads once the build is done. Tags never change, so a tag is built again only after the cap in point 6 dropped it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A remote source (``[user@]host:/path``) is returned as-is with the default target (its colon is the rsync host separator). Otherwise a colon suffix is a restore target only when absolute; a relative suffix is rejected here (device parses those itself)."
msgstr "Sumber jarak jauh (``[user@]host:/path``) dikembalikan sebagai - adalah dengan target baku (titik dua adalah pemisah host rsync). Jika tidak sebuah akhiran colon adalah sebuah target restore hanya ketika absolut; akhiran relatif ditolak di sini (perangkat parses mereka sendiri)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A rendered ``socialhome.toml`` is mounted alongside the environment file. It carries exactly one setting — ``[standalone].external_url`` — because that value has no ``SH_*`` environment equivalent upstream and federation pairing returns ``422 NOT_CONFIGURED`` without it."
msgstr "Sebuah render ``socialhome.toml`` dikaitkan dengan berkas lingkungan. Ini membawa tepat satu pengaturan - ``[standalone].external_url`` - karena nilai yang tidak ``SH_*`` lingkungan ekuivalen upstream dan pasangan federasi kembali ``422 NOT_CONFIGURED`` tanpa itu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A rendered `socialhome.toml` is mounted alongside the environment file. It carries exactly one setting — `[standalone].external_url` — because that value has no `SH_*` environment equivalent upstream and federation pairing returns `422 NOT_CONFIGURED` without it."
msgstr "Sebuah render `socialhome.toml` dikaitkan dengan berkas lingkungan. Ini membawa tepat satu pengaturan - `[standalone].external_url` - karena nilai yang tidak `SH_*` lingkungan ekuivalen upstream dan pasangan federasi kembali `422 NOT_CONFIGURED` tanpa itu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A repository definition must declare at least one of these; the rest (``name``, ``description``, ``gpgkey``, ``gpgcheck``, ``state``) qualify it."
msgstr "Sebuah definisi repositori harus mendeklarasikan paling tidak satu dari ini; sisanya (``name``, ``description``, ``gpgkey``, ``gpgcheck``, ``state``) Itu memenuhi syarat."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A repository is proxied by Nexus. A host is additionally answered for by the frontend, so a client keeps addressing its real upstream URL. `listen: [80]` serves it over plain HTTP and issues no certificate; `paths:` maps several repositories under one host; `mirror:` on a repository names the sibling the frontend retries against on `502`, `503` or `504`; `passthrough: true` suits an upstream that hands out URLs already carrying the repository prefix."
msgstr "A repositori is proxied by Nexus. Host tambahan yang dijawab oleh frontend, sehingga klien terus menangani yang nyata upstream URL. `listen: [80]` melayani itu atas HTTP biasa dan masalah tidak ada sertifikat; `paths:` memetakan beberapa repositori di bawah satu host; `mirror:` di nama repositori yang dipakai oleh saudara antarmuka untuk mengulang `502`, `503` atau `504`; `passthrough: true` cocok dengan suatu upstream yang membagikan URL telah membawa prefiks repositori."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A repository may serve several hosts and a host may be served by one repository only; a repository without a host is proxied but never hijacked, which is how a client that already addresses Nexus directly is served."
msgstr "Sebuah repositori mungkin melayani beberapa host dan host mungkin dilayani oleh satu repositori saja; sebuah repositori tanpa host yang proxied tapi tidak pernah dibajak, yang adalah bagaimana klien yang sudah alamat Nexus secara langsung dilayani."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A repository-local Sphinx entry point is also available at [Contribution Guide Index](docs/contributing/index.rst)."
msgstr "Sebuah repository- lokal titik masukan Sphinx juga tersedia di [Indeks Panduan Konfig](docs/contributing/index.rst)."

msgid "A request names one or more roles of that application from its `meta/rbac.yml` and carries a mandatory reason."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A request stays local while a local model can serve it, switch or not"
msgstr "Permintaan tetap lokal sementara model lokal dapat melayani itu, switch atau tidak"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A request whose demands exceed a model's capabilities never reaches it"
msgstr "Permintaan yang tuntutan melebihi kemampuan model tidak pernah mencapainya"

msgid "A requirement is a work package with a user story and a checklist of acceptance criteria. Every criterion carries a stable id; the ids and their proof kind are kept in the repository (`agents/criteria.yml`), so lints and scenarios never depend on the board being reachable."
msgstr ""

msgid "A restricted location (``services.sso.oauth2.restricted_locations``) redirects its 403 to the request page and preselects the roles of the location’s groups."
msgstr ""

msgid "A restricted location (`services.sso.oauth2.restricted_locations`) redirects its 403 to the request page and preselects the roles of the location's groups."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A retrigger inherits the window its source was given: the rows in front of that window were proven by the runs before it, and re-walking them from the head would redeploy a green stretch that nobody doubts. The source run's own ``offset`` input is that window's start."
msgstr "Sebuah retrigger mewarisi jendela sumbernya diberikan: baris di depan jendela itu terbukti oleh berjalan sebelum itu, dan kembali berjalan mereka dari kepala akan menyebarkan peregangan hijau bahwa tidak ada keraguan. Sumber run sendiri ``offset`` input adalah bahwa jendela itu dimulai."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A reusable [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) adapter, instantiated once per provider application. Each instance fronts exactly one upstream, holds only that upstream's least-privileged credential, and exposes only the operations its checked-in contract names."
msgstr "Sebuah dapat digunakan kembali [Protokol Konteks Model](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) adaptor, instantiated sekali setiap aplikasi penyedia. Setiap instance front persis satu hulu, memegang hanya bahwa ujung hulu - kredensial istimewa, dan mengekspos hanya operasi yang memeriksa-dalam nama kontrak."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A reusable `Model Context Protocol <https://modelcontextprotocol.io/>`__ adapter, instantiated once per provider application. Each instance fronts exactly one upstream, holds only that upstream’s least-privileged credential, and exposes only the operations its checked-in contract names."
msgstr "Sebuah dapat digunakan kembali `Model Context Protocol <https://modelcontextprotocol.io/>`__ adaptor, instantiated sekali setiap aplikasi penyedia. Setiap instance front persis satu hulu, memegang hanya bahwa ujung hulu - kredensial istimewa, dan mengekspos hanya operasi yang memeriksa-dalam nama kontrak."

msgid "A reviewed Weblate string wins over every engine"
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role MAY belong to more than one type. ``svc-opt-ssd-hdd`` is the canonical example: it declares both ``application_id`` and ``system_service_id`` and is therefore an application AND a system service. :func:`get_role_types` returns the full set so callers that care about scope (e.g. lint tests asserting \"this file is allowed for applications\") can use simple set membership."
msgstr "Sebuah peran MY milik lebih dari satu tipe. ``svc-opt-ssd-hdd`` adalah contoh kanonikal: ia menyatakan keduanya ``application_id`` dan ``system_service_id`` dan oleh karena itu aplikasi DAN layanan sistem. :func:`get_role_types` mengembalikan set lengkap sehingga penelepon yang peduli dengan scope (mis. tes lint asserting \"berkas ini diijinkan untuk aplikasi\") dapat menggunakan set sederhana keanggotaan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role MAY belong to several types simultaneously (for example an application that also ships a systemd unit). The returned frozenset contains every type whose marker matches; the user / tooling fallbacks fire only when no marker resolves."
msgstr "Sebuah MAY peran milik beberapa jenis secara bersamaan (Misalnya aplikasi yang juga mengirimkan unit sistemd). The return fingerset berisi setiap tipe yang penanda cocok; pengguna / tooling fallbacks hanya ketika tidak ada penanda pemecahan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role MAY omit the file entirely. The loader then exposes exactly one variant equal to the assembled per-role meta payload (`meta/services.yml` + `meta/server.yml` + `meta/rbac.yml` + `meta/volumes.yml` + `apply_schema()`'d `meta/secrets.yml`) unchanged."
msgstr "Sebuah peran MY menghilangkan file sepenuhnya. Pemuat kemudian mengekspos persis satu varian sama dengan dirakit muatan meta perrole (`meta/services.yml` + `meta/server.yml` + `meta/rbac.yml` + `meta/volumes.yml` + `apply_schema()`d `meta/secrets.yml`) tidak berubah."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "A role MAY ship `templates/design.js`, or `templates/design.js.j2` when it needs Jinja. `sys-front-inj-design` carries the per-app config `{logo, title, urls}` in the script tag's `data-design` attribute and prepends a line that reads it into `INFINITO_DESIGN`, collapses the result, adds its CSP hash and injects it whenever `services.design.enabled` is enabled, independent of `services.javascript.enabled`. The config rides in the attribute because CSP hashes only the script body: an onion vhost rewrites the CDN host in the payload, and a body holding that host would no longer match its hash. For the same reason a design script MUST read branding through `INFINITO_DESIGN` and MUST NOT interpolate `design.urls` itself."
msgstr ""

msgid "A role MUST NOT write an onion host by hand or rewrite hosts in its own proxy config."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role MUST be able to answer four questions clearly:"
msgstr "Sebuah peran HARUS dapat menjawab empat pertanyaan dengan jelas:"

msgid "A role aggregated to its id loses what actually broke: the retrigger then redeploys every variant of it, in whatever mode and network mode the sweep rotation happens to pick, and the combination that failed may not be among them. Each failed job therefore contributes its own ``role#variant@mode+network`` token (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`), so the priority line replays that job and nothing else."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role can be pulled into the inventory through any of three paths and they compose, not exclude one another:"
msgstr "Sebuah peran dapat ditarik ke dalam persediaan melalui salah satu dari tiga jalan dan mereka menyusun, tidak exclude satu sama lain:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role declares `meta/mcp.yml` when it actually serves or consumes MCP. The file is a capability descriptor, not a service entry: no single role provides MCP, so the service registry cannot pair provider and consumer, and the `mcp_consumer` flag in `meta/services.yml` does it instead. Vocabulary lives in [`utils/roles/applications/mcp.py`](../../../../../utils/roles/applications/mcp.py); the hard lint is [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py)."
msgstr "Sebuah peran menyatakan `meta/mcp.yml` ketika benar-benar melayani atau mengkonsumsi MCP. Berkas ini adalah deskripsi kapabilitas, bukan entri layanan: tidak ada peran tunggal yang menyediakan MCP, sehingga registri layanan tidak dapat memasangkan penyedia dan konsumen, dan `mcp_consumer` tanda in `meta/services.yml` melakukannya sebagai gantinya. Vokalisasi tinggal di [`utils/roles/applications/mcp.py`](../../../../../utils/roles/applications/mcp.py); garis keras adalah [`test_mcp_schema.py`](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_schema.py)."

# berbeda: ``README.md`` Mereka yang menyaksikan saling bertanya, "Adakah yang
