# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Amended after implementation: the deployed Hermes version serves a bearer API rather than a browser dashboard, so its native-OIDC support cannot be used. It is gated at the auth proxy instead, like OpenClaw and Flowise, admitting the role's `administrator` and `mcp` groups. Holding `API_SERVER_KEY` alone was the whole boundary before, which put every MCP provider Hermes is admitted to behind one shared deployment secret. The cost of the proxy is deliberate: an OpenAI-compatible client presenting only a bearer no longer reaches Hermes through its public vhost, and has to come from inside the container network."
msgstr "Diakui setelah implementasi: versi Hermes yang dipakai melayani pembawa API bukan dashboard browser, sehingga nativenya- OIDC dukungan tidak dapat digunakan. Hal ini gated di proxy auth bukan, seperti OpenClaw dan Flowise, mengakui peran `administrator` dan `mcp` kelompok. Memegang `API_SERVER_KEY` sendirian adalah batas sebelumnya, yang menempatkan setiap MCP penyedia Hermes diakui di balik satu rahasia penyebaran bersama. Biaya proksi ini disengaja: Klien OpenAI- yang hanya menyajikan pembawa yang tidak lagi mencapai Hermes melalui vhost publik, dan harus datang dari dalam jaringan kontainer."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Among the hosts in `svc-swarm-node`, the cluster manager is identified by additional membership in `svc-swarm-manager`. v1 scope: exactly ONE host. Workers are derived as `svc-swarm-node − svc-swarm-manager` — no duplicated list in `group_vars`."
msgstr "Di antara para host `svc-swarm-node`, manajer cluster diidentifikasi oleh keanggotaan tambahan di `svc-swarm-manager`. v1 scope: persis satu host. Pekerja diturunkan sebagai `svc-swarm-node − svc-swarm-manager` - tidak ada daftar duplikat dalam `group_vars`."

