msgid "An `ask` match pauses the routine (LangGraph interrupt) and asks the owner through a channel or Open WebUI. Approve resumes, reject or timeout aborts. A channel approval counts only when it comes from the owner's exact account on the local homeserver, carries the nonce bound to the hash of the requested action and its parameters, arrives before the nonce expires, and is the nonce's first use; reactions never count. Agents cannot write to `agents/firewall/` at runtime, and an override from Open WebUI can narrow but never widen a rule."
msgstr ""

