# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That choice is wrong in two directions at once. A prompt that needs a large context window reaches a model that cannot hold it, which is how [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) answers HTTP 500 when the agent model declares fewer than 64000 tokens. And a one-line factual question reaches whatever the deploy happened to pick, which is usually the largest model available."
msgstr "Pilihan itu salah dalam dua arah sekaligus. Sebuah prompt yang membutuhkan jendela konteks besar mencapai model yang tidak dapat menahannya, yaitu bagaimana [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) jawaban HTTP 500 ketika model agen mendeklarasikan lebih sedikit dari 64000 token. Dan pertanyaan faktual satu baris mencapai apa pun yang terjadi untuk memilih, yang biasanya model terbesar yang tersedia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That contract is wrong for one class of failure. When a value could not be measured and substituting one would be a guess, silence turns a loud stop into a wrong number nobody sees. Such a failure raises from here and every render layer re-raises it untouched."
msgstr "Kontrak itu salah untuk satu kelas kegagalan. Ketika nilai tidak dapat diukur dan diganti satu akan menebak, keheningan ternyata berhenti keras ke nomor yang salah tidak ada yang melihat. Kegagalan seperti itu muncul dari sini dan setiap lapisan render tidak tersentuh."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role's own run and this one. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "File itu membawa klien ke MCP yang diinginkan negara dari awal, sehingga file yang sama melayani peran sendiri menjalankan dan yang satu ini. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` gagal ketika peran klien kurang itu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role’s own run and this one. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "File itu membawa klien ke MCP yang diinginkan negara dari awal, sehingga file yang sama melayani peran sendiri menjalankan dan yang satu ini. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` gagal ketika peran klien kurang itu."

msgid "That is also what a retrigger replays: `--failed` reads the glyphs off the failed job's title and writes them back as a token, so the row comes back in the mode, network mode, distribution and architecture it died on rather than on whatever the rotation would pick next. The architecture is replayed because it is the machine the job ran on, not a preference it could fall back from. The filesystem is deliberately left out. A title states the kind the matrix *assigned*, which a deploy is allowed to fall back from, so pinning it would both misstate what the job ran on and turn the kind into a demand, failing the retrigger on the very condition the fallback absorbs."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is what stops the supervisor flow rather than effort. Flowise reaches an MCP server over the container network, and a stdio server has no address there: the client spawns and owns the process, so a shared endpoint two consumers could hold at once does not exist, and the deploy-time contract probe would consume the only session. Wrapping each agent in a stdio-to-HTTP bridge would put an unreviewed process on the platform's most privileged path — an agent with tool access — to work around a transport upstream has not shipped, which is the workaround this project refuses. Re-review when either upstream serves MCP over HTTP."
msgstr "Itulah yang menghentikan aliran pengawas daripada usaha. Flowise mencapai server MCP melalui jaringan kontainer, dan server STdio tidak memiliki alamat di sana: spawns klien dan memiliki proses, sehingga titik akhir yang sama dua konsumen bisa terus sekaligus tidak ada, dan penyediaan kontrak waktu probe akan mengkonsumsi satu-satunya sesi. Membungkus setiap agen dalam jembatan stdio- HTTP akan menempatkan proses yang tidak diulas pada platform yang paling istimewa jalan - seorang agen dengan akses alat - untuk bekerja sekitar transportasi upstream belum dikirim, yang merupakan solusi sekitar proyek ini menolak. Ulasan ulang ketika baik upstream melayani MCP atas HTTP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why the repo favors:"
msgstr "Itulah mengapa repo nikmat:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why the repo has:"
msgstr "Itulah mengapa repo memiliki:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why you will find host work in `sys-*` roles and app work in `web-app-*` roles instead of one giant deployment script."
msgstr "Itulah mengapa Anda akan menemukan tuan rumah bekerja di `sys-*` peran dan aplikasi bekerja `web-app-*` peran bukan satu naskah penyebaran raksasa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That last step is deliberately the deployed [`sys-ctl-hlth-container` script](../../../sys-ctl-hlth-container/files/shell/script.sh) rather than a check of the drill's own: it is what watches the host in production, it knows swarm services, and it dumps 200 log lines per sick container. It is invoked as a script, not as its systemd unit — the unit's `OnFailure` starts the soft-repair service, and a drill that repairs what it found has stopped measuring. It cannot replace the drill's own wait either: a container that never came back is in no `container ps` filter, so only the recorded-set check sees it."
msgstr "Langkah terakhir itu sengaja digunakan [`sys-ctl-hlth-container` skrip](../../../sys-ctl-hlth-container/files/shell/script.sh) bukan cek sendiri bor: itu adalah apa yang menonton tuan rumah dalam produksi, ia tahu layanan kerumunan, dan itu kesedihan 200 log baris per kontainer sakit. Hal ini dipanggil sebagai script, bukan sebagai unit sistemnya - unit `OnFailure` memulai layanan perbaikan perlahan, dan bor yang memperbaiki apa yang ditemukan telah berhenti mengukur. Hal ini tidak dapat menggantikan menunggu bor sendiri baik: sebuah wadah yang tidak pernah kembali adalah dalam tidak `container ps` filter, jadi hanya recorded- set cek melihatnya."

