msgid "The pieces `evict.py` builds on: the shared and model cache units with their link grouping ([units.py](eviction/units.py)), the Nexus REST client and its `.env` reader ([nexus.py](eviction/nexus.py)), and the Docker build-cache and running-tool probes ([docker.py](eviction/docker.py))."
msgstr ""

msgid "The pin does not by itself carry the OIDC back-channel on an onion node. libcurl refuses a `.onion` name in `Curl_resolv()` before it reads its own cache or `/etc/hosts` (curl 8.5.0 `lib/hostip.c:694-701`), so the token, JWKS and userinfo calls `auth_oidc` makes through Moodle's `\\curl` never leave the container. `MOODLE_OIDC_SOCKS_PROXY` therefore exports `http_proxy`, `https_proxy` and `no_proxy` into `.env/env` whenever the Keycloak domain ends in `.onion`: libcurl reads the lowercase names, `socks5h://` hands the name to Tor to resolve, and on a clearnet issuer the three keys are not rendered at all. The FPM pool keeps `clear_env = no`, which is what puts the container environment in front of libcurl, and only the `moodle` and `cron` services read `.env/env`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The pin does not by itself carry the OIDC back-channel on an onion node. libcurl refuses a ``.onion`` name in ``Curl_resolv()`` before it reads its own cache or ``/etc/hosts`` (curl 8.5.0 ``lib/hostip.c:694-701``), so the token, JWKS and userinfo calls ``auth_oidc`` makes through Moodle’s ``\\curl`` never leave the container. ``MOODLE_OIDC_SOCKS_PROXY`` therefore exports ``http_proxy``, ``https_proxy`` and ``no_proxy`` into ``.env/env`` whenever the Keycloak domain ends in ``.onion``: libcurl reads the lowercase names, ``socks5h://`` hands the name to Tor to resolve, and on a clearnet issuer the three keys are not rendered at all. The FPM pool keeps ``clear_env = no``, which is what puts the container environment in front of libcurl, and only the ``moodle`` and ``cron`` services read ``.env/env``."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The pin lives in ``[project.optional-dependencies].dev`` (one SPOT, Dependabot keeps it current). Host venvs, the lint container and CI all read that same pin, so a rule that is preview-gated in one release and stable in the next (e.g. ISC004, or S310 firing on ``urllib.request.Request``) cannot disagree across environments."
msgstr "Pin tinggal di ``[project.optional-dependencies].dev`` (satu SPOT, Dependabot menyimpannya saat ini). Host venvs, container lint dan CI semua membaca pin yang sama, sehingga sebuah aturan yang dipreview-gated dalam satu rilis dan stabil di berikutnya (mis. ISC004, atau S310 menembak ``urllib.request.Request``) tidak bisa tidak setuju di seluruh lingkungan."

msgid "The pin stays anyway, and removing it as redundant breaks the login again: `\\core\\files\\curl_security_helper::host_is_blocked()` performs a forward `gethostbynamel()` whenever any IP rule is configured and returns blocked when the name does not resolve, so without `/etc/hosts` the Keycloak authority is rejected inside Moodle before libcurl is reached."
msgstr ""

msgid "The pin stays anyway, and removing it as redundant breaks the login again: ``\\core\\files\\curl_security_helper::host_is_blocked()`` performs a forward ``gethostbynamel()`` whenever any IP rule is configured and returns blocked when the name does not resolve, so without ``/etc/hosts`` the Keycloak authority is rejected inside Moodle before libcurl is reached."
