msgid "The post-login assertion MUST prove the session is real, in this order of preference: a user-menu or persona-name string visible in the DOM, a navigation element only rendered for authenticated users, a URL pattern unique to authenticated state. Stopping at a 2xx status code or a static text snippet that exists logged-out as well MUST NOT count as a session check."
msgstr "Pernyataan post- login Must membuktikan sesi ini nyata, dalam urutan preferensi: sebuah menu atau string nama-pribadi terlihat dalam DOM, sebuah elemen navigasi hanya diberikan untuk pengguna terotentikasi, sebuah pola URL unik ke keadaan yang terotentikasi. Berhenti di 2kode status xx atau snippet teks statis yang ada log-out juga HARUS TIDAK dihitung sebagai pemeriksaan sesi."

msgid "The pre-create takes absence only from an exact name in `network ls`; any failed probe fails the deploy. A network of that name must be an attachable swarm overlay on the pinned subnet, with the configured encryption and the provider's namespace, or the deploy fails and asks to remove it. Encryption is the presence of the `encrypted` option (moby `daemon/libnetwork/drivers/overlay/ov_network.go:119-121` checks only the key), so the option is left out when `swarm.network.encryption` is off."
msgstr ""

msgid "The pre-fill is `\"{{ lookup('tor_egress_infrastructure') }}\"`, a global lookup over `services.tor.egress.infrastructure` (`mirrors`, `ntp`, `registry_blob_hosts`, `acme`). The applications payload renders every role's configuration in every role's context, so a role-local lookup or a role variable would not resolve outside svc-net-tor. Registries are derived from the images of the applications in `group_names`; the mirrors and time servers are one list for all supported distributions, because host facts are not reliably present when the payload renders; ACME and the blob hosts are declared, because no configuration names them. A registry port is stripped, and `localhost`, `*.localhost` and address registries are skipped. The lookup returns an empty list off a Tor node and on a malformed block and never raises, because the payload renders it on every host; the role validates the block in `tasks/00_core.yml`."
msgstr ""

