msgid "Trusted fork PRs: a maintainer-applied *trusted-pr* label runs a fork PR as deliberately released code — the orchestrator skips the fork-prerequisite wait and the privileged *pull_request_target* build switches its source from the base merge ref to the raw PR head, while the built image keeps the merge-SHA tag so every downstream consumer is unchanged. The label is the only switch (applying a label is collaborator-only on GitHub, so fork authors cannot grant it), build-orchestration scripts always come from the base repository, and both unlabeled fork PRs and same-repository PRs are untouched. See [the fork-PR pipeline](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) and [the contributor fork workflow](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."
msgstr "PRS garpu terpercaya: seorang penjaga -diterapkan *trusted- pr* label menjalankan sebuah humas fork sebagai sengaja dirilis kode - yang antristrator melewati fork- prasyarat tunggu dan hak istimewa *pull_request_target* membuat switch sumber dari basis penggabungan ref ke kepala PR mentah, sedangkan citra dibangun terus merge- SHA tag sehingga setiap konsumen hilir tidak berubah. Label adalah satu-satunya switch (menerapkan sebuah label adalah kolaborator- hanya di GitHub, jadi penulis fork tidak dapat mengabulkannya), skrip archestration build- selalu berasal dari repositori dasar, dan baik park PRs maupun same- repositori PRs tidak tersentuh. Lihat [baris pipa fork-PR](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) dan [alur kerja garpu kontributor](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."

msgid "Trusted measurement sources: the `profile_tasks` timestamp line gives the duration of the previous task, so pair a `TASK` header with the next timestamp line; the `TASKS RECAP` and `Playbook run took` totals; the two per-target wall-clock tables; the pytest summary lines and the `FAILED TARGETS:` line."
msgstr ""

msgid "Trusted sources: the `profile_tasks` timestamp line is the previous task's duration, so a `TASK` header pairs with the next timestamp; the `TASKS RECAP` and `Playbook run took` totals; the two per-target wall-clock tables; the pytest summary and the `FAILED TARGETS:` line. The make exit code is never a verdict, and a quality gate whose test phase is red never runs its lint phase."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Trusted-header SSO bridge migration"
msgstr "Migrasi jembatan SSO-header"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Trusted-header single-sign-on bridges (wave 1) for *web-app-openproject*, *web-app-snipe-it*, *web-app-postmarks* and *web-app-yourls*, with *web-app-baserow* and *web-app-bookwyrm* migrating to the header bridge and dropping their LDAP configuration. The shared proxy (*sys-svc-proxy*) now strips forgeable identity headers on every location to close trusted-header injection."
msgstr "Trust-header single-signs pada jembatan (gelombang 1) untuk *web-app-openproject*, *web-app-snipe-it*, *web-app-postmarks* dan *web-app-yourls*, dengan *web-app-baserow* dan *web-app-bookwyrm* bermigrasi ke jembatan header dan menjatuhkan konfigurasi LDAP mereka. Proksi terbagi (*sys-svc-proxy*) sekarang strip forgable identitas header pada setiap lokasi untuk menutup trust-header injeksi."

msgid "Trusted-proxy sources: `gateway.trustedProxies` names the front proxy's address pool (`NETWORK_ROLE_SUBNET_POOL` in compose, Docker's default overlay pool in swarm), not its exact source address. Cause: compose reaches the published port through the gateway of whichever role network Docker binds the port to, and the swarm overlay of `svc-prx-openresty` has no fixed subnet, so no lookup returns that address. Forged identities are refused by the proxy-owned secret header in `requiredHeaders` regardless. Options: a shared lookup that returns the front proxy's source address per deployment mode (a fixed IPAM subnet for the openresty overlay, a pinned gateway network for published ports)."
msgstr ""

