# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[mapping.py](../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py) is the only authoritative location for this schema. It exposes the path constants, the `ROLE_FILES` dict that scopes each path per role type, and the `mandatory`, `allowed` and `marker` flags that drive both lint enforcement and role-type detection. Every consumer (lint tests, role-type detection, the CLI documented below) MUST read from this file. Adding a new role type or a new role file MUST happen here first; the rest of the system reads the dict at runtime."
msgstr "[mapping.py](../../../../utils/roles/mapping.py) adalah satu-satunya lokasi yang berwenang untuk skema ini. Ini mengekspos konstanta jalan, yang `ROLE_FILES` titik yang melihat setiap jalur per tipe peran, dan `mandatory`, `allowed` dan `marker` tanda yang mendorong penegakan benang dan deteksi ROLE-type. Setiap konsumen (Uji warna, deteksi jenis role-, dokumen CLI di bawah) Harus dibaca dari file ini. Menambahkan tipe peran baru atau berkas peran baru HARUS terjadi di sini pertama; sisa sistem membaca dekrit pada waktu-jalan."

msgid "[meta/lifecycle.yml](../../../../../meta/lifecycle.yml) is the SPOT for every status: its `description`, its `predecessors`, its reference-rule `flags` (`production`, `retired`), the CI trigger `contexts` that deploy it (`ci-deploy`), the `actions` the system takes on a role in it, and the `migrations` exemptions. Consumers read it through [utils/roles/lifecycle.py](../../../../../utils/roles/lifecycle.py); no consumer spells a status list of its own. The linear order below is derived from the predecessor graph, which MUST be acyclic, have exactly one entry, reach every status and sort into exactly one order; [test_lifecycle_spot.py](../../../../../tests/lint/repository/test_lifecycle_spot.py) enforces that."
msgstr ""

