# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_MAX_AGE_MIN` (default `8640` = 6 days) controls how long every Nexus proxy repo holds an upstream response before revalidating. The bootstrap helper applies it as `contentMaxAge`, `metadataMaxAge`, and `negativeCache.timeToLive`. The default is intentionally one day below the 7-day `Valid-Until` window Debian and Ubuntu generate in their apt `Release` files, so Nexus always refreshes the manifest before `apt-get update` would see it expired. Raise it for slow-moving upstreams when staleness is preferable to upstream load; lower it further for fast-moving feeds (`apt-debian-security`, branch-pinned tarballs) when staleness becomes visible."
msgstr "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_MAX_AGE_MIN` (baku `8640` = 6 hari) control how long every Nexus proxy repo holds an upstream response before revalidating. Bootstrap helper berlaku sebagai `contentMaxAge`, `metadataMaxAge`, dan `negativeCache.timeToLive`. Baku sengaja satu hari di bawah 7-hari `Valid-Until` jendela Debian dan Ubuntu menghasilkan apt mereka `Release` file, so Nexus always refresh the manifest before `apt-get update` akan melihatnya berakhir. Naikkan untuk memperlambat-bergerak upstream ketika stalness lebih baik untuk upstream load; lebih rendah lebih lanjut untuk cepat-bergerak feed (`apt-debian-security`, branch-pinned tarballs) ketika keteduhan menjadi terlihat."

