# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh api` switches implicitly from GET to POST as soon as a body-flag is present; no explicit `-X`/`--method` is required. Without these ask rules the broad `Bash(*)` allow would let body-carrying `gh api` POSTs through silently. Short forms (`-f`, `-F`), long forms (`--field`, `--raw-field`), and file input (`--input`) are all listed so no spelling slips past. A future gh-CLI body-flag would need to be added here explicitly."
msgstr "`gh api` switch implisit from GET to POST as soon as a body- flag is present; no explisit `-X`/`--method` diperlukan. Tanpa ini meminta aturan luas `Bash(*)` memungkinkan akan membiarkan tubuh-membawa `gh api` Tetap tenang. Bentuk pendek (`-f`, `-F`), bentuk panjang (`--field`, `--raw-field`), dan masukan berkas (`--input`) semuanya terdaftar jadi tidak ada spelling slip masa lalu. Sebuah hantu masa depan Cli bendera perlu ditambahkan di sini secara eksplisit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` plants a binary that runs the next time any `gh` subcommand opens an editor (e.g. `gh issue create` without `--body`), a deferred-execution backdoor that survives the current session. Persistent CLI config belongs to a deliberate operator decision."
msgstr "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` tanaman biner yang berjalan waktu berikutnya setiap `gh` subcommand membuka suatu penyunting (mis. `gh issue create` tanpa `--body`), sebuah backdoor eksekusi dikurangi yang bertahan sesi saat ini. CLI yang gigih percaya milik keputusan operator yang disengaja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh` CLI's cache directory (HTTP response cache + extension metadata). Granted because every `gh` invocation writes cache entries at startup; denying it would require every `gh` call to be wrapped with an `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, which adds a shell shape that falls out of sandbox auto-allow and forces per-subcommand allow entries. Auth tokens are **not** stored here (they live in `~/.config/gh/`, which stays read-only). Persistence trade-off is identical to `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache poisoning, if it occurred, would survive reboots, but API auth is server-side so the blast radius is bounded to wrong-output-to-operator."
msgstr "`gh` Direktori cache CLI (Metadata respon HTTP + ekstensi). Memang karena setiap `gh` pemanggilan menulis masukan cache di startup; menyangkal itu akan membutuhkan setiap `gh` panggilan untuk dibungkus dengan `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, yang menambahkan bentuk shell yang keluar dari sandbox auto- memungkinkan dan memaksa per- subcommand memungkinkan entri. Token buah selalu **tidak** disimpan di sini (mereka tinggal di `~/.config/gh/`, yang tetap baca-saja)Ketekunan adalah identik dengan `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache keracunan, jika itu terjadi, akan bertahan reboot, tapi API auth adalah sisi server- jadi radius ledakan dibatasi untuk salah - outputt -to-operator."

